{"id":"29b6e85c7e08bdf163cb3888a5bc60873e7536d7","axis":"silent","repo":"nrwl/nx","sha":"29b6e85c7e08bdf163cb3888a5bc60873e7536d7","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"astro-docs/src/content/docs/kb/split-e2e-tasks.mdoc","lines":["@@ -504,6 +504,12 @@ Add the test file's task to `project.json` under its name, with two changes to t","           \"projects\": [\"checkout\", \"checkout-utils\"],","           \"always\": true,","         },","+        {","+          \"input\": \"production\",","+          \"projects\": [\"checkout\", \"checkout-utils\"],","+          \"dependencies\": true,","+          \"always\": true,","+        },","         { \"externalDependencies\": [\"cypress\"] },","       ],","       \"dependsOn\": [","@@ -514,7 +520,7 @@ Add the test file's task to `project.json` under its name, with two changes to t"," }"," ```"," ","-- `^production` becomes an input that selects only the listed projects. With `\"always\": true`, [ultracache keeps their files in the hash](/docs/reference/inputs#inputs-kept-under-ultracache).","+- `^production` becomes two inputs. The first selects the listed projects, and the second, with `\"dependencies\": true`, selects the projects they depend on. With `\"always\": true`, [ultracache keeps their files in the hash](/docs/reference/inputs#inputs-kept-under-ultracache)."," - The dependency on the web server task sets [`\"inputs\": false`](/docs/reference/inputs#inputs-of-continuous-dependencies), so the server's inputs stop counting."," "," `inputs` and `dependsOn` in `project.json` replace the arrays the plugin infers, so list every entry you keep.","@@ -524,7 +530,7 @@ The task name comes from the test file's path. When you move or rename the file,"," "," ### Scope a task with a comment in the test file"," ","-For Cypress and Playwright atomized tasks, you can name the projects in an `@nx-depends-on` comment at the top of the test file instead:","+For Cypress, Playwright, and Jest atomized tasks, you can name the projects in an `@nx-depends-on` comment at the top of the test file instead:"," "," ```ts"," // apps/shop-e2e/src/e2e/checkout.cy.ts","@@ -539,15 +545,16 @@ The scope moves with the test file, and a new test file opts in with its own com"," Nx reads the comment from the comment block at the top of the file and stops at the first line of code."," Nx ignores a comment without projects and logs a warning that names the test file."," When Playwright starts the web server itself, there's no server task, so only the inputs change.","+Jest atomized tasks have no server task either, so only their inputs change."," Test files without the comment keep the inferred configuration."," "," ### What counts after scoping"," "," These rules apply to both ways of scoping:"," ","-- Only the listed projects count as dependency inputs, not the projects they depend on.","+- The listed projects and the projects they depend on count as dependency inputs."," - The task keeps its other declared inputs, such as `default` and any shared globs it includes."," - Under ultracache, the files the test read during its recorded run replace the declared file inputs, except the `always` ones."," - A change outside the remaining inputs leaves the task's hash unchanged, so Nx replays the cached result.","-- A listed name that matches no project is an error, but a missing project goes unnoticed, so list every project the test relies on.","+- A listed name that matches no project is an error. A project left off the list goes unnoticed unless a listed project depends on it, so list every project the test exercises."," - With `NX_LEGACY_AFFECTED=false`, `nx affected` selects the task by these inputs. Without it, `nx affected` selects whole projects."],"additions":11,"deletions":4,"truncated":false},{"path":"astro-docs/src/content/docs/reference/inputs.mdoc","lines":["@@ -412,6 +412,19 @@ You can reference named inputs from specific projects or from project dependenci"," "," The `projects` property can be a string or an array of strings specifying which project(s) to reference the named input from. Using just the string name (e.g., `\"production\"`) is shorthand for referencing the named input from the current project. Prefixing with `^` (e.g., `\"^production\"`) references the named input from all project dependencies."," ","+Add `\"dependencies\": true` to a `projects` input to reference the named input from the dependencies of those projects.","+For each listed project, these are the files its own `^production` covers.","+The listed projects themselves don't count, so pair it with the plain form to cover a project and everything it depends on:","+","+```jsonc","+{","+  \"inputs\": [","+    { \"input\": \"production\", \"projects\": \"myapp\" },","+    { \"input\": \"production\", \"projects\": \"myapp\", \"dependencies\": true },","+  ],","+}","+```","+"," {% aside type=\"note\" title=\"^ with filesets vs named inputs\" %}"," The `^` prefix behaves differently depending on what follows it:"," "],"additions":13,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"astro-docs/src/content/docs/technologies/test-tools/jest/introduction.mdoc","lines":["@@ -211,6 +211,9 @@ Use two plugin entries to separate unit and E2E Jest tasks, and enable CI splitt"," Here `ciTargetName` atomizes only the E2E tasks."," Use `ciGroupName` to set a custom group label."," ","+To stop an atomized task from rerunning for every library the project depends on, scope it to the projects its test file exercises.","+See [scope a test file to its projects](/docs/kb/split-e2e-tasks#scope-a-test-file-to-its-projects).","+"," ### View inferred tasks"," "," Open the project details view in Nx Console or run:"],"additions":3,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/cypress/src/plugins/plugin.spec.ts","lines":["@@ -726,6 +726,12 @@ describe('@nx/cypress/plugin', () => {","           projects: ['feature', 'feature-utils'],","           always: true,","         },","+        {","+          input: 'production',","+          pr